 https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Chjb!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4bb113f6-349a-432a-83ea-ce94e834b4dd_830x663.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>I am spending some time to try and check if I got it right. My friend George Smith works on tools for math education and I\u2019m trying to use his generated problems to gain a better intuition of what GPT Sol actually did. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png\" width=\"862\" height=\"573\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:573,&quot;width&quot;:862,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:81442,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/i/210781831?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KYcM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F583b96e2-5a7f-47a9-bb6e-5039217d3c72_862x573.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>I am well aware of being wrong, so <strong>I have emailed the authors of this paper to check to see if it makes sense</strong>. Formalising it feels to heavy as a tool right now, so I\u2019ll stick to algebra tools. I will disclose in a later post if I have found that I have made mistakes. </p><p>Here are some notes on what I\u2019m looking for when I try to make AI assisted proofs</p><ul><li><p>Find a problem that I can understand. </p><ul><li><p>This feels really important, what\u2019s the point of doing research math if you don\u2019t get the joy of trying to understand something new?</p><ul><li><p>If you choose problems that you understand you will be more likely to somewhat be invested in the solution and also be more likely to take it in a useful place. </p></li><li><p>The concepts you learn are more likely to mentally hook to something you care about which might make some cool second order effects. </p></li><li><p>If you choose a problem you understand you will feel good when its solved, which I rate highly. </p></li><li><p>A lot of results in maths aren\u2019t applicable to real life, the search space is huge, just chill. </p></li><li><p>Somehow I feel more drawn to math that has some empiricism in scope, or a model of the world that is not obvious. </p></li></ul></li></ul></li><li><p>If you understand more math you are more likely to have an expanded universe of problems that feel significant (and can hopefully solve with AI assistance) </p><ul><li><p>This means that it is still worth trying to understand math.</p></li><li><p>It feels more likely to me that one part of the future of math is trying to digest results made by AI and trying to see if they have wider significance. </p></li><li><p>I still think people want to understand things, I still find understanding things fun and knowing how things work is fun. I don\u2019t think it matters if something is already known, there are infinitely many presentations of knowledge that can be valuable in different ways. </p></li><li><p>I still think there is scope for a much needed, much better thought out way of communicating and storing such results. </p></li></ul></li></ul><h4>Acknowledgements </h4><p>Thanks to George Smith for the discussions. All mistakes are mine.</p><p>Proof</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"2950\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:2950,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:679050,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/i/210781831?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff8175dd1-f4ee-45af-ae72-3d8eae6fc9bd_1706x3456.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BWrP!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,